IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Securities and Futures Act 2001 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation (a rendering, not the official text).
-- s 4: "interest in securities, securities-based derivatives contracts or units in collective investment scheme".
-- One function per route to an interest (subsections (1), (3), (4), (5), (7), (8)), one for each rule that something is immaterial
-- ((2), (9)), one for each disregarded interest ((10)(a) to (f)), one for the rule that three reasons do not justify disregarding (11),
-- and one function that combines them. Imports prelude and daydate only.
--
-- "The thing" below is the security, securities-based derivatives contract or unit in a collective investment scheme the interest is in.
-- Whether it is one of those is the Act's rule in sfa-definitions-products.l4 and sfa-definitions-schemes.l4; here it is one yes/no input.
--
-- Reading (a) of the brief (a failed "if" is the text's no, clause by clause) carries every JUST FALSE below that is not a flat negative.
-- Each such branch is marked `-- MARGINAL-READING (a)` and listed in NOTES.md; the other reading is NOTHING.
--
-- How to read a function in this module.
--   Every defined term of s 2(1) is ONE function, named `s 2(1) "<term>" <the thing> is <the term>`, over the facts a person could state.
--   The result is MAYBE BOOLEAN:
--     JUST TRUE   the thing is within the term (a limb of the definition is met and no exclusion applies);
--     JUST FALSE  the TEXT says it is not: a definition that says "means" and no limb is met, or an express exclusion ("but does not include");
--     NOTHING     the text does not say: an "includes" definition (an open list) with no listed limb met.
--   A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
--   Every branch that answers "no" carries `-- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "..."`; every branch that
--   answers "not covered" carries `-- NOTHING-kind (<why>)`.
--   A limb the Act hands to the Authority, the regulations or another Act ("prescribed", "specified", "as defined in the
--   Banking Act 1970") is an INPUT named for the fact ("the Authority has prescribed ..."), never a thing read from memory.
--   The definitions apply "unless the context otherwise requires" (the chapeau of s 2(1)): that qualification is
--   `s 2(1) the definitions apply unless the context otherwise requires` in sfa-definitions-rest.l4, not repeated here.

§ `s 4: interest in securities, securities-based derivatives contracts or units`

-- src:3783 | 4.—(1) Subject to this section, a person has an interest in securities,
-- src:3784 | securities‑based derivatives contracts or units in a collective
-- src:3785 | investment scheme, if the person has authority (whether formal or
-- src:3786 | informal, or express or implied) to dispose of, or to exercise control
-- src:3787 | over the disposal of, those securities, securities‑based derivatives
-- src:3788 | contracts or units in a collective investment scheme, as the case may
-- src:3789 | be.
@ref s 4(1) (src:3783-3789)
GIVEN
    `the person has authority to dispose of the thing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person have authority (formal or informal, express or implied) to dispose of the security, securities-based derivatives contract or unit in a collective investment scheme?
    `the person has authority to exercise control over the disposal of the thing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person have authority (formal or informal, express or implied) to exercise control over the disposal of the security, securities-based derivatives contract or unit in a collective investment scheme?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(1) the person has authority over the disposal of the thing` MEANS
    IF `the person has authority to dispose of the thing` OR `the person has authority to exercise control over the disposal of the thing`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person has an interest in securities, securities-based derivatives contracts or units in a collective investment scheme, if the person has authority (whether formal or informal, or express or implied) to dispose of, or to exercise control over the disposal of, those securities, securities-based derivatives contracts or units in a collective investment scheme"
    -- MARGINAL-READING (a): the text gives this as a sufficient condition ("if") and subsection (1) is "Subject to this section"; a failed "if" is taken as the text's no for this route. The other reading is NOTHING.

@ref s 4(1) (the combining function) (src:3783-3789)
GIVEN
    `the thing is a security, a securities-based derivatives contract or a unit in a collective investment scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing a security, a securities-based derivatives contract or a unit in a collective investment scheme (as section 2(1) defines those)?
    `the person has an interest by the route of s 4(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for s 4(1) answer (authority to dispose of, or control the disposal of, the thing)? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `the person has an interest by the route of s 4(3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for s 4(3) answer (a trust)? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `the person has an interest by the route of s 4(4)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for s 4(4) answer (a corporation the person directs or controls)? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `the person has an interest by the route of s 4(5)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for s 4(5) answer (a corporation in which the person and associates hold 20% of the votes)? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `the person has an interest by the route of s 4(7)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for s 4(7) answer (one of the circumstances in subsection (7))? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `the person has an interest by the route of s 4(8)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for s 4(8) answer (joint holding)? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `the interest is to be disregarded under section 4(10)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does `s 4(10) the interest is to be disregarded` answer for this interest? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4 the person has an interest in the securities, securities-based derivatives contracts or units` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the thing is a security, a securities-based derivatives contract or a unit in a collective investment scheme`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): section 4 speaks of "securities, securities-based derivatives contracts or units in a collective investment scheme"
        IF `the interest is to be disregarded under section 4(10)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to this section, a person has an interest in securities ... if ...; (10) The following interests are to be disregarded"
        IF (`the person has an interest by the route of s 4(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`the person has an interest by the route of s 4(3)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`the person has an interest by the route of s 4(4)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`the person has an interest by the route of s 4(5)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`the person has an interest by the route of s 4(7)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`the person has an interest by the route of s 4(8)` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (`the person has an interest by the route of s 4(1)` EQUALS NOTHING) OR (`the person has an interest by the route of s 4(3)` EQUALS NOTHING) OR (`the person has an interest by the route of s 4(4)` EQUALS NOTHING) OR (`the person has an interest by the route of s 4(5)` EQUALS NOTHING) OR (`the person has an interest by the route of s 4(7)` EQUALS NOTHING) OR (`the person has an interest by the route of s 4(8)` EQUALS NOTHING)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a route the caller could not answer, so the text is not applied to it
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to this section, a person has an interest in securities, securities-based derivatives contracts or units in a collective investment scheme, if the person has authority"
        -- MARGINAL-READING (a): every route is an "if" or "treated as" condition and none says "only"; with every route failed the text is taken to say no. The other reading is NOTHING.

-- src:3793 | (2) For the purposes of subsection (1), it is immaterial that the
-- src:3794 | authority of a person to dispose of, or to exercise control over the
-- src:3795 | disposal of, particular securities, securities‑based derivatives
-- src:3796 | contracts or units in a collective investment scheme (as the case
-- src:3797 | may be) is, or is capable of being made, subject to restraint or
-- src:3798 | restriction.
@ref s 4(2) (src:3793-3798)
GIVEN
    `the authority is, or is capable of being made, subject to restraint or restriction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person's authority to dispose of, or to exercise control over the disposal of, the security, securities-based derivatives contract or unit in a collective investment scheme subject, or capable of being made subject, to restraint or restriction?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(2) it is immaterial that the authority is subject to restraint or restriction` MEANS
    IF `the authority is, or is capable of being made, subject to restraint or restriction`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): with no restraint there is nothing for subsection (2) to make immaterial

-- src:3802 | (3) Where any property held in trust consists of or includes
-- src:3803 | securities, securities‑based derivatives contracts or units in a
-- src:3804 | collective investment scheme, and a person knows, or has
-- src:3805 | reasonable grounds for believing, that the person has an interest
-- src:3806 | under the trust, the person is treated as having an interest in those
-- src:3807 | securities, securities‑based derivatives contracts or units in a
-- src:3808 | collective investment scheme, as the case may be.
@ref s 4(3) (src:3802-3808)
GIVEN
    `property held in trust consists of or includes the thing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does property held in trust consist of, or include, the security, securities-based derivatives contract or unit in a collective investment scheme?
    `the person knows, or has reasonable grounds for believing, that the person has an interest under the trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person know, or have reasonable grounds for believing, that the person has an interest under the trust?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(3) the person is treated as having an interest through a trust` MEANS
    IF `property held in trust consists of or includes the thing` AND `the person knows, or has reasonable grounds for believing, that the person has an interest under the trust`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where any property held in trust consists of or includes securities, securities-based derivatives contracts or units in a collective investment scheme, and a person knows, or has reasonable grounds for believing, that the person has an interest under the trust, the person is treated as having an interest in those securities, securities-based derivatives contracts or units in a collective investment scheme"
    -- Guide, periods ruling of 2026-11-05, rule (b): a "where ..." condition, when it fails, answers JUST FALSE.

-- src:3812 | (4) A person is treated as having an interest in a security,
-- src:3813 | securities‑based derivatives contract or unit in a collective
-- src:3814 | investment scheme if a corporation has, or is by the provisions of
-- src:3815 | this section treated as having, an interest in that security,
-- src:3816 | securities‑based derivatives contract or unit in a collective
-- src:3817 | investment scheme (as the case may be) and —
-- src:3819 | (a) the corporation is, or its directors are, accustomed or under
-- src:3820 | an obligation, whether formal or informal, to act in
-- src:3821 | accordance with the directions, instructions or wishes of
-- src:3822 | the person; or
-- src:3827 | (b) the person has a controlling interest in the corporation.
@ref s 4(4) (src:3812-3827)
GIVEN
    `a corporation has, or is by section 4 treated as having, an interest in the thing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a corporation have, or is it by the provisions of section 4 treated as having, an interest in the security, securities-based derivatives contract or unit in a collective investment scheme?
    `the corporation is, or its directors are, accustomed or under an obligation to act in accordance with the directions, instructions or wishes of the person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation, or are its directors, accustomed or under an obligation (formal or informal) to act in accordance with the directions, instructions or wishes of the person?
    `the person has a controlling interest in the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person have a controlling interest in the corporation? (The text does not define "controlling interest": say what you consider it to be.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(4) the person is treated as having an interest through a corporation the person directs or controls` MEANS
    IF `a corporation has, or is by section 4 treated as having, an interest in the thing` AND (`the corporation is, or its directors are, accustomed or under an obligation to act in accordance with the directions, instructions or wishes of the person` OR `the person has a controlling interest in the corporation`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person is treated as having an interest in a security, securities-based derivatives contract or unit in a collective investment scheme if a corporation has, or is by the provisions of this section treated as having, an interest in that security, securities-based derivatives contract or unit in a collective investment scheme (as the case may be) and"
    -- MARGINAL-READING (a): an "if" condition; a failed "if" is taken as the text's no for this route. The other reading is NOTHING.

-- src:3833 | (5) A person is treated as having an interest in a security,
-- src:3834 | securities‑based derivatives contract or unit in a collective
-- src:3835 | investment scheme if —
-- src:3837 | (a) a corporation has, or is by the provisions of this section
-- src:3838 | (apart from this subsection) treated as having, an interest in
-- src:3839 | that security, securities‑based derivatives contract or unit
-- src:3840 | in a collective investment scheme, as the case may be; and
-- src:3842 | (b) the person, the associates of the person, or the person and
-- src:3843 | the person’s associates are entitled to exercise or control
-- src:3844 | the exercise of not less than 20% of the votes attached to
-- src:3845 | the voting shares in the corporation.
@ref s 4(5) (src:3833-3845)
GIVEN
    `a corporation has, or is by section 4 (apart from subsection (5)) treated as having, an interest in the thing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a corporation have, or is it by the provisions of section 4 (apart from subsection (5)) treated as having, an interest in the security, securities-based derivatives contract or unit in a collective investment scheme?
    `the votes attached to the voting shares in the corporation that the person, the person's associates, or both are entitled to exercise or control` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of the votes attached to the voting shares in the corporation are the person, the person's associates (as subsection (6) has it), or the person and the associates together entitled to exercise or control the exercise of?
    `the total votes attached to the voting shares in the corporation` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes in total are attached to the voting shares in the corporation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(5) the person is treated as having an interest through a corporation in which the person and associates hold 20% of the votes` MEANS
    IF `a corporation has, or is by section 4 (apart from subsection (5)) treated as having, an interest in the thing` AND (`the total votes attached to the voting shares in the corporation` GREATER THAN 0) AND ((`the votes attached to the voting shares in the corporation that the person, the person's associates, or both are entitled to exercise or control` TIMES 100) AT LEAST (`the total votes attached to the voting shares in the corporation` TIMES 20))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person is treated as having an interest in a security, securities-based derivatives contract or unit in a collective investment scheme if (a) a corporation has, or is by the provisions of this section (apart from this subsection) treated as having, an interest in that security, securities-based derivatives contract or unit in a collective investment scheme, as the case may be; and (b) the person, the associates of the person, or the person and the person's associates are entitled to exercise or control the exercise of not less than 20% of the votes attached to the voting shares in the corporation"
    -- MARGINAL-READING (a): an "if" condition; a failed "if" is taken as the text's no for this route. The other reading is NOTHING.
    -- Assumed, not ruled: a corporation with no votes at all (the total is 0) has no "20% of the votes", so the route fails.

-- src:3849 | (6) For the purposes of subsection (5), a person is an associate of
-- src:3850 | another person if the firstmentioned person is —
-- src:3852 | (a) a subsidiary of that other person;
-- src:3854 | (b) a person who is accustomed or is under an obligation
-- src:3855 | whether formal or informal to act in accordance with the
-- src:3856 | directions, instructions or wishes of that other person in
-- src:3857 | relation to the security, securities‑based derivatives
-- src:3858 | contract or unit in a collective investment scheme (as the
-- src:3859 | case may be) referred to in subsection (5); or
-- src:3861 | (c) a corporation that is, or a majority of the directors of which
-- src:3862 | are, accustomed or under an obligation whether formal or
-- src:3863 | informal to act in accordance with the directions,
-- src:3864 | instructions or wishes of that other person in relation to
-- src:3865 | that security, securities‑based derivatives contract or unit
-- src:3866 | in a collective investment scheme, as the case may be.
@ref s 4(6) (src:3849-3866)
GIVEN
    `the person is a subsidiary of the other person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a subsidiary of the other person (as section 2(1) "subsidiary" has it)?
    `the person is accustomed or under an obligation to act in accordance with the directions, instructions or wishes of the other person in relation to the thing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person accustomed, or under an obligation (formal or informal), to act in accordance with the directions, instructions or wishes of the other person in relation to the security, securities-based derivatives contract or unit in a collective investment scheme referred to in subsection (5)?
    `the person is a corporation that is, or a majority of whose directors are, accustomed or under an obligation to act in accordance with the other person's directions in relation to the thing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a corporation that is, or a majority of the directors of which are, accustomed or under an obligation (formal or informal) to act in accordance with the directions, instructions or wishes of the other person in relation to that thing?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(6) the person is an associate of the other person for the purposes of subsection (5)` MEANS
    IF `the person is a subsidiary of the other person` OR `the person is accustomed or under an obligation to act in accordance with the directions, instructions or wishes of the other person in relation to the thing` OR `the person is a corporation that is, or a majority of whose directors are, accustomed or under an obligation to act in accordance with the other person's directions in relation to the thing`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "For the purposes of subsection (5), a person is an associate of another person if the firstmentioned person is (a) a subsidiary of that other person; (b) a person who is accustomed or is under an obligation whether formal or informal to act in accordance with the directions, instructions or wishes of that other person in relation to the security, securities-based derivatives contract or unit in a collective investment scheme (as the case may be) referred to in subsection (5); or (c) a corporation that is, or a majority of the directors of which are, accustomed or under an obligation whether formal or informal to act in accordance with the directions, instructions or wishes of that other person in relation to that security, securities-based derivatives contract or unit in a collective investment scheme, as the case may be"
    -- MARGINAL-READING (a): an "if" condition; a failed "if" is taken as the text's no. The other reading is NOTHING.

-- src:3870 | (7) A person is treated as having an interest in a security,
-- src:3871 | securities‑based derivatives contract or unit in a collective
-- src:3872 | investment scheme in any one or more of the following
-- src:3873 | circumstances:
@ref s 4(7) (src:3870-3873)
GIVEN
    `the circumstance in paragraph (a) is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for section 4(7)(a) answer?
    `the circumstance in paragraph (b) is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for section 4(7)(b) answer?
    `the circumstance in paragraph (c) is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for section 4(7)(c) answer?
    `the circumstance in paragraph (d) is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for section 4(7)(d) answer?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(7) the person is treated as having an interest in one of the circumstances` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the circumstance in paragraph (a) is met` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`the circumstance in paragraph (b) is met` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`the circumstance in paragraph (c) is met` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`the circumstance in paragraph (d) is met` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (`the circumstance in paragraph (a) is met` EQUALS NOTHING) OR (`the circumstance in paragraph (b) is met` EQUALS NOTHING) OR (`the circumstance in paragraph (c) is met` EQUALS NOTHING) OR (`the circumstance in paragraph (d) is met` EQUALS NOTHING)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a circumstance the caller could not answer, so the text is not applied to it
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person is treated as having an interest in a security, securities-based derivatives contract or unit in a collective investment scheme in any one or more of the following circumstances"
        -- MARGINAL-READING (a): "in any one or more of the following circumstances" is read as a sufficient condition like "if"; with no circumstance met this route fails. The other reading is NOTHING.

-- src:3878 | (a) where the person has entered into a contract to purchase the
-- src:3879 | security, securities‑based derivatives contract or unit in a
-- src:3880 | collective investment scheme, as the case may be;
@ref s 4(7)(a) (src:3878-3880)
GIVEN
    `the person has entered into a contract to purchase the thing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person entered into a contract to purchase the security, securities-based derivatives contract or unit in a collective investment scheme?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(7)(a) the person has entered into a contract to purchase the thing` MEANS
    IF `the person has entered into a contract to purchase the thing`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person is treated as having an interest in a security, securities-based derivatives contract or unit in a collective investment scheme in any one or more of the following circumstances (a) where the person has entered into a contract to purchase the security, securities-based derivatives contract or unit in a collective investment scheme, as the case may be"
    -- Guide, periods ruling of 2026-11-05, rule (b): a "where ..." condition, when it fails, answers JUST FALSE.

-- src:3882 | (b) where the person has a right, otherwise than by reason of
-- src:3883 | having an interest under a trust, to have the security,
-- src:3884 | securities‑based derivatives contract or unit in a collective
-- src:3885 | investment scheme (as the case may be), transferred to the
-- src:3886 | person or to the person’s order, whether the right is
-- src:3887 | exercisable presently or in the future and whether on the
-- src:3888 | fulfilment of a condition or not;
@ref s 4(7)(b) (src:3882-3888)
GIVEN
    `the person has a right to have the thing transferred to the person or to the person's order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person have a right (exercisable presently or in the future, and whether on the fulfilment of a condition or not) to have the security, securities-based derivatives contract or unit in a collective investment scheme transferred to the person or to the person's order?
    `the right is by reason of the person having an interest under a trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person have that right by reason of having an interest under a trust?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(7)(b) the person has a right to have the thing transferred to the person or to the person's order` MEANS
    IF `the person has a right to have the thing transferred to the person or to the person's order` AND (NOT `the right is by reason of the person having an interest under a trust`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) where the person has a right, otherwise than by reason of having an interest under a trust, to have the security, securities-based derivatives contract or unit in a collective investment scheme (as the case may be), transferred to the person or to the person's order, whether the right is exercisable presently or in the future and whether on the fulfilment of a condition or not"
    -- Guide, periods ruling of 2026-11-05, rule (b): a "where ..." condition, when it fails, answers JUST FALSE.

-- src:3890 | (c) where the person has the right to acquire any of the
-- src:3891 | following under an option, whether the right is exercisable
-- src:3892 | presently or in the future and whether on the fulfilment of a
-- src:3893 | condition or not:
-- src:3895 | (i) the security, securities‑based derivatives contract or
-- src:3896 | unit in a collective investment scheme, as the case
-- src:3897 | may be;
-- src:3899 | (ii) an interest in the security, securities‑based
-- src:3900 | derivatives contract or unit in a collective
-- src:3901 | investment scheme, as the case may be;
@ref s 4(7)(c) (src:3890-3901)
GIVEN
    `the person has the right to acquire the thing under an option` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person have the right to acquire the security, securities-based derivatives contract or unit in a collective investment scheme under an option, whether the right is exercisable presently or in the future and whether on the fulfilment of a condition or not?
    `the person has the right to acquire an interest in the thing under an option` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person have the right to acquire an interest in the security, securities-based derivatives contract or unit in a collective investment scheme under an option, whether the right is exercisable presently or in the future and whether on the fulfilment of a condition or not?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(7)(c) the person has the right to acquire the thing, or an interest in it, under an option` MEANS
    IF `the person has the right to acquire the thing under an option` OR `the person has the right to acquire an interest in the thing under an option`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(c) where the person has the right to acquire any of the following under an option, whether the right is exercisable presently or in the future and whether on the fulfilment of a condition or not (i) the security, securities-based derivatives contract or unit in a collective investment scheme, as the case may be; (ii) an interest in the security, securities-based derivatives contract or unit in a collective investment scheme, as the case may be"
    -- Guide, periods ruling of 2026-11-05, rule (b): a "where ..." condition, when it fails, answers JUST FALSE.

-- src:3903 | (d) where the person is entitled, otherwise than by reason of
-- src:3904 | the person having been appointed a proxy or representative
-- src:3905 | to vote at a meeting of members of a corporation or of a
-- src:3906 | class of its members, to exercise or control the exercise of a
-- src:3907 | right attached to any of the following, as the case may be:
-- src:3909 | (i) the security, not being a security of which the person
-- src:3910 | is a registered holder;
-- src:3912 | (ii) the securities‑based derivatives contract, not being a
-- src:3913 | contract to which the person is a party;
-- src:3915 | (iii) the unit in a collective investment scheme, not being
-- src:3916 | a unit of which the person is a registered holder.
@ref s 4(7)(d) (src:3903-3916)
GIVEN
    `the person is entitled to exercise, or to control the exercise of, a right attached to the thing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person entitled to exercise, or to control the exercise of, a right attached to the security, securities-based derivatives contract or unit in a collective investment scheme?
    `the person is entitled only by reason of having been appointed a proxy or representative to vote at a meeting of members of a corporation or of a class of its members` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person entitled only by reason of having been appointed a proxy or representative to vote at a meeting of members of a corporation, or of a class of its members?
    `the person is the registered holder of the security or unit, or a party to the securities-based derivatives contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person the registered holder of the security or of the unit in a collective investment scheme, or a party to the securities-based derivatives contract?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(7)(d) the person is entitled to exercise or control the exercise of a right attached to the thing` MEANS
    IF `the person is entitled to exercise, or to control the exercise of, a right attached to the thing` AND (NOT `the person is entitled only by reason of having been appointed a proxy or representative to vote at a meeting of members of a corporation or of a class of its members`) AND (NOT `the person is the registered holder of the security or unit, or a party to the securities-based derivatives contract`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(d) where the person is entitled, otherwise than by reason of the person having been appointed a proxy or representative to vote at a meeting of members of a corporation or of a class of its members, to exercise or control the exercise of a right attached to any of the following, as the case may be (i) the security, not being a security of which the person is a registered holder; (ii) the securities-based derivatives contract, not being a contract to which the person is a party; (iii) the unit in a collective investment scheme, not being a unit of which the person is a registered holder"
    -- Guide, periods ruling of 2026-11-05, rule (b): a "where ..." condition, when it fails, answers JUST FALSE.

-- src:3920 | (8) A person is treated as having an interest in a security,
-- src:3921 | securities‑based derivatives contract or unit in a collective
-- src:3922 | investment scheme if that security, securities‑based derivatives
-- src:3927 | contract or unit in a collective investment scheme (as the case may
-- src:3928 | be) is held jointly by the person with another person.
@ref s 4(8) (src:3920-3928)
GIVEN
    `the thing is held jointly by the person with another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the security, securities-based derivatives contract or unit in a collective investment scheme held jointly by the person with another person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(8) the thing is held jointly by the person with another person` MEANS
    IF `the thing is held jointly by the person with another person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person is treated as having an interest in a security, securities-based derivatives contract or unit in a collective investment scheme if that security, securities-based derivatives contract or unit in a collective investment scheme (as the case may be) is held jointly by the person with another person"
    -- MARGINAL-READING (a): an "if" condition; a failed "if" is taken as the text's no for this route. The other reading is NOTHING.

-- src:3932 | (9) For the purpose of determining whether a person has an interest
-- src:3933 | in a security, securities‑based derivatives contract or unit in a
-- src:3934 | collective investment scheme, it is immaterial that the interest cannot
-- src:3935 | be related to a particular security, securities‑based derivatives
-- src:3936 | contract or unit in a collective investment scheme, as the case may be.
@ref s 4(9) (src:3932-3936)
GIVEN
    `the interest cannot be related to a particular security, securities-based derivatives contract or unit in a collective investment scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the interest cannot be related to a particular security, securities-based derivatives contract or unit in a collective investment scheme?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(9) it is immaterial that the interest cannot be related to a particular thing` MEANS
    IF `the interest cannot be related to a particular security, securities-based derivatives contract or unit in a collective investment scheme`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): an interest that can be related to a particular thing is outside what subsection (9) says

-- src:3940 | (10) The following interests are to be disregarded:
@ref s 4(10) (src:3940-3940)
GIVEN
    `the interest is within paragraph (a) of section 4(10)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for section 4(10)(a) answer?
    `the interest is within paragraph (b) of section 4(10)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for section 4(10)(b) answer?
    `the interest is within paragraph (c) of section 4(10)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for section 4(10)(c) answer?
    `the interest is within paragraph (d) of section 4(10)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for section 4(10)(d) answer?
    `the interest is within paragraph (e) of section 4(10)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for section 4(10)(e) answer?
    `the interest is within paragraph (f) of section 4(10)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for section 4(10)(f) answer?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(10) the interest is to be disregarded` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the interest is within paragraph (a) of section 4(10)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`the interest is within paragraph (b) of section 4(10)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`the interest is within paragraph (c) of section 4(10)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`the interest is within paragraph (d) of section 4(10)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`the interest is within paragraph (e) of section 4(10)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`the interest is within paragraph (f) of section 4(10)` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (`the interest is within paragraph (a) of section 4(10)` EQUALS NOTHING) OR (`the interest is within paragraph (b) of section 4(10)` EQUALS NOTHING) OR (`the interest is within paragraph (c) of section 4(10)` EQUALS NOTHING) OR (`the interest is within paragraph (d) of section 4(10)` EQUALS NOTHING) OR (`the interest is within paragraph (e) of section 4(10)` EQUALS NOTHING) OR (`the interest is within paragraph (f) of section 4(10)` EQUALS NOTHING)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a limb the caller could not answer, so the text is not applied to it
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The following interests are to be disregarded"
        -- MARGINAL-READING (a): the list is introduced without "only"; with no limb met, each limb's "if" has failed and the text is taken to say no. The other reading is NOTHING (list not closed).

