-- src:3984 | (11) An interest in a security, securities‑based derivatives contract
-- src:3985 | or unit in a collective investment scheme is not to be disregarded by
-- src:3986 | reason only of —
-- src:3988 | (a) its remoteness;
-- src:3990 | (b) the manner in which it arose; or
-- src:3992 | (c) the fact that the exercise of a right conferred by the interest
-- src:3993 | is, or is capable of being made subject to restraint or
-- src:3994 | restriction.
@ref s 4(11) (src:3984-3994)
GIVEN
    `the ground for disregarding the interest is its remoteness` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is one ground for disregarding the interest its remoteness?
    `the ground for disregarding the interest is the manner in which it arose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is one ground for disregarding the interest the manner in which it arose?
    `the ground for disregarding the interest is that the exercise of a right conferred by the interest is, or is capable of being made, subject to restraint or restriction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is one ground for disregarding the interest that the exercise of a right conferred by the interest is, or is capable of being made, subject to restraint or restriction?
    `there is some other ground for disregarding the interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there any other ground for disregarding the interest?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(11) the interest is to be disregarded by reason only of its remoteness, how it arose, or restraint` MEANS
    IF (`the ground for disregarding the interest is its remoteness` OR `the ground for disregarding the interest is the manner in which it arose` OR `the ground for disregarding the interest is that the exercise of a right conferred by the interest is, or is capable of being made, subject to restraint or restriction`) AND (NOT `there is some other ground for disregarding the interest`)
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An interest in a security, securities-based derivatives contract or unit in a collective investment scheme is not to be disregarded by reason only of (a) its remoteness; (b) the manner in which it arose; or (c) the fact that the exercise of a right conferred by the interest is, or is capable of being made subject to restraint or restriction"
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by reason only of"; a ground outside (a) to (c) is outside subsection (11)
